From: dinadur <59811564+dinadur@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 12:16:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/20] B70: travel controller v3 pin; one delivery-error
 message; fresh run_dir on reruns

- ACCEPTED_TRAVEL_CONTROLLER_SHA256 -> 1cd021b3 (controller v3: a malformed
  review chunk keeps its valid entries and retries in halves instead of
  quarantining every venue in it).
- TRAVEL_RESEARCH_DELIVERY_ERROR is no longer pushed through
  stream_delta_callback. Telegram showed it twice (the streamed copy, then the
  final send with the failed-turn footer) on the 2026-10-08 Charleston and
  Sedona reruns. Same fix as the approval preview in d73362e.
- The runner moves a reused, non-empty run_dir to a new <name>-rerun-N
  sibling instead of failing with "run_dir must be new or empty", which spent
  the turn's single controller attempt on reruns of a destination. The used
  directory is untouched, the request validation stays strict, and the runner
  prints a TRAVEL_RESEARCH_RUNNER_NOTE line before any controller output.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
